      "question": "Should I release the brake when it pulses during emergency braking?",
      "canonical_answer": "The manual says not to release the brake lever/pedal when pulsations occur during hard braking in an emergency; these indicate ABS activation. Apply both brakes simultaneously. ABS does not substitute for careful riding or anticipation and does not reduce braking distance; in some circumstances it can lengthen it. Ride and brake carefully, especially while cornering. Anticipate the stopping distance for your speed and brake well in advance. The instrument cluster must function properly as it is integral to ABS. Failing to follow these cautions can cause an accident with serious injury or loss of life.",
