          "full_record_text": "# EXP015 v4 - Rolled-over engine shutdown\r\n\r\nGenerated based on feedback from the first 11 cases.\r\n\r\nManual: Royal Enfield Himalayan BS6 owner's manual, RAM00818/A,4 November2025.\r\nSHA-256: cf221a29e2f9cd5af6e80a99774a697c814e8eda661c27d72e519d8a7e80da89.\r\nType: conditional source action. Risk: high.\r\nOriginal source: PDF 68,79-80; printed 66,77-78. Original page text and author-rendered complete-page contact sheets inspected where available. This is author inspection only; reviewer must independently inspect exact full pages, continuations, tables, figures, and required warning scope. PDF103 intentionally remains an extraction/source-review gap. No retrieval result used as proof.\r\n\r\nProposed engineering conversation:\r\n\r\nRider: \"The bike fell on its side with the engine running in gear and then stopped.\"\r\n\r\nAssistant: \"The manual describes roll-over-sensor shutdown in that situation. Before its reset, the bike must be safely upright on its centre stand on firm flat ground, in neutral with the neutral lamp glowing. Take extreme care: a fall can injure you or others and damage the bike. Only do this once the motorcycle is already securely supported. The reset guidance does not provide instructions for lifting a fallen bike or safely placing it on the stand. If you can safely confirm those conditions, switch both ignition and stop switches OFF, wait a few seconds, then switch them ON. This does not establish that the bike is undamaged or safe to ride; if condition after the fall is uncertain, have authorised service inspect it.\"\r\n\r\nFollow-up conversations/outcomes: Cannot safely right/support bike: withhold reset and obtain assistance. Unknown gear/neutral: clarify before action. Reset unresolved: service, no repeated loops. Reported restart does not close damage concerns. Starting procedure not supplied by this card.\r\n\r\nExact review checks and source limits: Centre-stand surface firm/flat and no injury/damage clearance claimed. Any actual cranking requires complete separately reviewed start procedure including75.\r\n\r\nScope: DRAFT tuning/regression only; no human approval, release, cached answer or runtime authority. Confirm Himalayan+BS6 selection and exact manual/checksum first. Actual controls/variant mismatch blocks action. Direct facts need approved complete evidence just as actions do. Page references are author provenance, not immutable runtime evidence IDs. Source excerpts and figures remain engineering-only; no new public PDF/crop permission.\r\n\r\nState and stops (PRODUCT_POLICY): keep missing/unclear facts UNKNOWN; normal observations never prove hidden system health. Preserve ACTION_COMPLETED_UNRESOLVED separately, avoid unjustified repeats, and retain separate open issues after customer-reported resolution. Never claim field repair verified. Table order is not OEM diagnostic order. Missing source dependencies block generation and cannot be solved by rider questions. Distinguish SUPPORTED/AMBIGUOUS/UNSUPPORTED/SAFETY_STOP/SYSTEM_ERROR under TRDv0.4. Explicit OEM service stops dominate additional checks. Support wording: Kindly write to Royal Enfield at support@royalenfield.com.\r\n\r\nRevision provenance: owner-requested origin declaration added; previous frozen content preserved. This provenance does not imply approval.\r\n\r\nRevision provenance: Agent2 source/experience feedback on v1; v2 only added owner provenance, now substantive v3. Exact latest review required.\r\n\r\nRevision provenance: reviewer/judge practical-discovery and rider-language corrections; original frozen version preserved.\r\n"
