      "exact_text": "Royal Enfield Himalayan\n83\nMINOR MAINTENANCE TIPS\n\nCheck that the oil level is between the minimum and\nmaximum lines on the sight glass.\n\nIf not, top up the oil level so that it is between the mini-\nmum and maximum lines on the sight glass\n\nReﬁll the specified fresh engine oil quantity 2.1 L.\nOIL FILTER REPLACEMENT   \n\nRemove the oil filter cover with O-ring and spring.\n\nRemove and discard the oil filter.\n\nAllow the oil to drain from the oil filter housing.\n\nThoroughly clean the cover and the O-ring sealing sur-\nface.\n\nInstall a new oil filter. Use the O-ring and lubricate the\nO-ring in the filter cover with water based lubricant.\n\nInstall the cover and tighten to 22±2 Nm, ensuring\nspring is retained in the cover.\n",
