      "exact_text": "Royal Enfield Himalayan\n102\nMINOR MAINTENANCE TIPS\nBATTERY AND MAINTENANCE\n\nThe motorcycle is provided with 12 V - 8 Ah VRLA\nbattery.\n\nThe battery must be periodically checked for cleanli-\nness and corrosion free terminals.\nNOTE\nThe poor contact or loose ﬁtment of battery terminals may\ncause ECU failure.\nDISMANTLING\n\nSwitch “OFF” the engine and remove ignition key from\nthe key barrel.\n\nThe battery is located underneath the rider seat.\n\nRemove the pillion and rider seat as per procedure.\n\nDisconnect battery black negative (-ve) terminal bolt\nby using 10 mm spanner available in the tool kit.\n\nDisconnect battery red positive (+ve) terminal bolt by\nusing 10 mm spanner available in the tool kit.\n",
