      "exact_text": "Royal Enfield Himalayan\n101\nMINOR MAINTENANCE TIPS\n6.The difference between values in step 4 and step 5\nshould be the drive chain free play is 35 to 40 mm. \n7. If the drive chain free play is found to be incorrect adjust\nas follows:\n(a) Loosen the rear wheel spindle.\n(b) Push the rear wheel to the extreme front in the swing\narm slot.\n(c) Turn the adjusting Allen bolt in small increments\nevenly on both sides, until the specified slackness is\nachieved. Wheel position in the slot on both sides\nshould always be kept equal between left and right.\n(d) Tighten the wheel spindle torque value is 70 Nm and\ntighten the adjusting Allen bolt torque value is 10 Nm.\nRecheck the slackness in the chain to confirm it, if it’s\nstill not within specification, repeat the adjustment\nprocedure first three steps.\nWARNING\n\nChain slackness beyond the specified limit will lead to\nchain slippage and may also cause increased wear rates\nto chain and sprockets.\n\nPlease ensure the both wheels are aligned correctly,\nafter adjusting the chain and before tightening the rear\nwheel spindle nut.\n",
