      "evidence_id": "originalpdf_d80e00ebbb9ff57f5d7469ed",
      "exact_text": "Royal Enfield Himalayan\n70\nSTARTING\n\nTo shift into neutral, move the motorcycle back and\nforth gently, while simultaneously shifting the gear.\nEnsure gear is in neutral position and the neutral lamp\nis glowing in the instrument cluster.\n\nTurn ignition key to ON position and engine kill switch\non right hand side handle bar to run position.\n\nWhen both the ignition and engine kill switch is in “ON”\nposition and after the vehicle is started, the MIL will\nglow for a few seconds and turns “OFF”, this indicates\nthat all the function of the electronic fuel injection (EFI)\nsystem is functioning normally. In the event of any\nmalfunction in the EFI system the MIL will glow contin-\nuously.\n",
