      ],
      "version": "TRD-v0.4"
    },
    "policy_c7c59d8b2e592d93c2827123": {
      "authority": "PRODUCT_POLICY",
      "evidence_id": "policy_c7c59d8b2e592d93c2827123",
      "exact_text": "This specification describes a version-locked, layout-aware multimodal RAG pipeline using only the supplied Royal Enfield New Himalayan 450 owner's manual with diagnostic session state. The LLM may translate a customer report into structured observations and paraphrase manual-backed instructions. No model may author a new repair step absent an applicable evidence object.",
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "source_path": "03_TRD.docx",
      "source_sha256": "aeedf6789ddfbddc674c1926c5d4441a27708bd260c673d876a5ff7fdb3792ac",
      "text_sha256": "028103230a113f9f20ce47065f55bd4bc935dfe6673f85d62e7e5daed205802b",
      "text_span": [
        0,
        373
      ],
      "version": "TRD-v0.4"
    },
    "policy_cff5c1033095e5d1045f7870": {
      "authority": "PRODUCT_POLICY",
      "evidence_id": "policy_cff5c1033095e5d1045f7870",
      "exact_text": "No permanent public-demo storage of image/audio by default; avoid putting raw media or personal text into traces",
      "paragraph_index": 149,
      "source_path": "03_TRD.docx",
      "source_sha256": "aeedf6789ddfbddc674c1926c5d4441a27708bd260c673d876a5ff7fdb3792ac",
      "text_sha256": "c8ea9642f1db20333e20f433fbe7e8e943e8acd0c55144f0c048a59b468da683",
      "text_span": [
        0,
        112
      ],
      "version": "TRD-v0.4"
    },
    "policy_d4d80b8ce114ff2b56a9f89b": {
      "authority": "PRODUCT_POLICY",
      "evidence_id": "policy_d4d80b8ce114ff2b56a9f89b",
      "exact_text": "Register manual: OEM, model, year range, variant, document edition, original URL, local hash SHA-256, language and rights status",
      "paragraph_index": 32,
      "source_path": "03_TRD.docx",
      "source_sha256": "aeedf6789ddfbddc674c1926c5d4441a27708bd260c673d876a5ff7fdb3792ac",
      "text_sha256": "b8684d3449a4ab6101afcc077a5b7f22e86d0826e38e27e64095e0024ed93457",
      "text_span": [
        0,
        128
      ],
      "version": "TRD-v0.4"
    },
    "policy_dec1ae94d172ff6ececb1329": {
      "authority": "PRODUCT_POLICY",
      "evidence_id": "policy_dec1ae94d172ff6ececb1329",
      "exact_text": "Apply two layers: a deterministic rules gate (valid manual, cited evidence IDs, required dependencies, prerequisites/variant, no explicit conflict) plus a semantic support evaluator that compares each proposed technical claim against relevant source spans. Reject the draft if either layer fails.",
      "paragraph_index": 127,
      "source_path": "03_TRD.docx",
      "source_sha256": "aeedf6789ddfbddc674c1926c5d4441a27708bd260c673d876a5ff7fdb3792ac",
      "text_sha256": "a3772faf1949c7ddd85457ffbcd9b4cb6a8cf5c0db3cf0acd8b0b2a746439255",
      "text_span": [
        0,
        296
      ],
      "version": "TRD-v0.4"
    },
    "policy_e27e55df4b38f7ac71faa0df": {
      "authority": "PRODUCT_POLICY",
      "evidence_id": "policy_e27e55df4b38f7ac71faa0df",
      "exact_text": "An action becomes eligible only when the manual and variant match, the rule is approved, the symptom or documented branch applies, required conditions and prerequisites are true, no applicable safety rule prohibits it, and the attempt history allows it. Evaluate the evidence-completeness and answer-release gates separately before issuing technical text. A direct factual lookup uses the same applicability and evidence gates without fabricating a diagnostic step.",
      "paragraph_index": 99,
      "source_path": "03_TRD.docx",
      "source_sha256": "aeedf6789ddfbddc674c1926c5d4441a27708bd260c673d876a5ff7fdb3792ac",
      "text_sha256": "9742e679a7c7a0f7e54651bd2a4480c4b438aa8969527169b021c26eb8f9bed1",
      "text_span": [
        0,
        465
      ],
      "version": "TRD-v0.4"
    },
    "policy_e32def2849e8ebb8db96208e": {
      "authority": "PRODUCT_POLICY",
      "evidence_id": "policy_e32def2849e8ebb8db96208e",
      "exact_text": "Operational failures in embedding, retrieval, assembly or the cross-encoder yield SYSTEM_ERROR with a typed error class and recorded attempts. A query exceeding the current cross-encoder's 128-token input bound, or work exceeding 100 query/passage pairs, skips that inference with an explicit reason and keeps ranking unresolved. Preserve the full query and source text; never silently truncate a rider report or mandatory evidence. A source gap cannot be resolved by asking the rider to supply a missing manual warning or table header.",
      "paragraph_index": 86,
      "source_path": "03_TRD.docx",
      "source_sha256": "aeedf6789ddfbddc674c1926c5d4441a27708bd260c673d876a5ff7fdb3792ac",
      "text_sha256": "887c4250fd52c98178072975733a636b979012b9302b9ce2ab610422ec634fb7",
      "text_span": [
        0,
        536
      ],
      "version": "TRD-v0.4"
    },
    "policy_e35a7c3a16450b052abb9d64": {
      "authority": "PRODUCT_POLICY",
      "evidence_id": "policy_e35a7c3a16450b052abb9d64",
      "exact_text": "The normal request path uses conditional reranking. Clearly ordered candidates with complete reviewed dependencies continue to the eligibility and answer gates. Reranking handles uncertain ordering among plausible candidates; evidence recovery handles required objects absent from the initial bundle. Similarity, RRF and cross-encoder scores cannot prove support or approve a procedure.",
      "paragraph_index": 82,
      "source_path": "03_TRD.docx",
      "source_sha256": "aeedf6789ddfbddc674c1926c5d4441a27708bd260c673d876a5ff7fdb3792ac",
      "text_sha256": "6158ab0925ebe25c260bf1721aaebc084be44d521c874fc164ce24f2414dd7e1",
      "text_span": [
        0,
        386
      ],
      "version": "TRD-v0.4"
    },
    "policy_e7e1b991bd3b8087d1bba5d3": {
      "authority": "PRODUCT_POLICY",
      "evidence_id": "policy_e7e1b991bd3b8087d1bba5d3",
      "exact_text": "Safety warnings take precedence over ordinary branch selection; unsupported safe workarounds are forbidden",
      "paragraph_index": 122,
      "source_path": "03_TRD.docx",
      "source_sha256": "aeedf6789ddfbddc674c1926c5d4441a27708bd260c673d876a5ff7fdb3792ac",
      "text_sha256": "43a409ce6a2038d76e0e19f4567b021751cf7beca1fc6c52c605eb3d3f455e53",
      "text_span": [
        0,
        106
      ],
      "version": "TRD-v0.4"
    },
    "policy_e978314f8b1f0dc0999a0ec4": {
      "authority": "PRODUCT_POLICY",
      "evidence_id": "policy_e978314f8b1f0dc0999a0ec4",
      "exact_text": "The controller selects the response route from structured eligibility decisions, the evidence bundle and gate results. A known applicable stop condition yields SAFETY_STOP and retains its verified warning even if other processing fails. Otherwise, a required component failure yields SYSTEM_ERROR. A resolvable missing applicability fact or documented branch observation yields AMBIGUOUS and one focused question. After bounded recovery, an unsupported request, an unresolved source gap or exhausted documented paths yields UNSUPPORTED with the verified support route.",
      "paragraph_index": 129,
      "source_path": "03_TRD.docx",
      "source_sha256": "aeedf6789ddfbddc674c1926c5d4441a27708bd260c673d876a5ff7fdb3792ac",
      "text_sha256": "8b8c624ef8cb5a4ad58d07753b305b79b3ca86576de82a3fbaffab1d8f1a65ff",
      "text_span": [
        0,
        568
      ],
      "version": "TRD-v0.4"
    },
    "policy_ef6c370e2ea29b0712b652b3": {
      "authority": "PRODUCT_POLICY",
      "evidence_id": "policy_ef6c370e2ea29b0712b652b3",
      "exact_text": "Prefer explicit OEM NEXT_STEP order; when no explicit order exists, only recommend another independently documented eligible check and do not imply OEM prioritization",
      "paragraph_index": 112,
      "source_path": "03_TRD.docx",
      "source_sha256": "aeedf6789ddfbddc674c1926c5d4441a27708bd260c673d876a5ff7fdb3792ac",
      "text_sha256": "ffeded245a6d497ea9342c99452b9a712d5aa9e26aebe0f53d2a343c7c186dd6",
      "text_span": [
        0,
        166
      ],
      "version": "TRD-v0.4"
    },
    "policy_f1879d328c71680eb537fe1a": {
      "authority": "PRODUCT_POLICY",
      "evidence_id": "policy_f1879d328c71680eb537fe1a",
      "exact_text": "TRD v0.4 is the authoritative design and technical contract as of 9 October 2026. This document follows it. The approved owner manual governs motorcycle facts; source applicability, rights, independent review and release gates remain mandatory. Recorded implementation progress does not constitute release approval.",
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "source_path": "03_TRD.docx",
      "source_sha256": "aeedf6789ddfbddc674c1926c5d4441a27708bd260c673d876a5ff7fdb3792ac",
      "text_sha256": "b47e1ff6fb68854d5eaac0687525a65b081a378b3ef7d75e784781f498846a9d",
      "text_span": [
        0,
        315
      ],
      "version": "TRD-v0.4"
    },
    "policy_f196384f650ba83df2a81a1f": {
      "authority": "PRODUCT_POLICY",
      "evidence_id": "policy_f196384f650ba83df2a81a1f",
      "exact_text": "When the manual lists possible causes or independently documented checks without branch conditions or an explicit next-step order, preserve those limits. Do not infer a condition, eliminate an undocumented branch, diagnose a fault from a negative clue or claim an OEM ranking from retrieval scores. The existing SM-04 policy governs selecting among independently documented eligible checks.",
      "paragraph_index": 96,
      "source_path": "03_TRD.docx",
      "source_sha256": "aeedf6789ddfbddc674c1926c5d4441a27708bd260c673d876a5ff7fdb3792ac",
      "text_sha256": "931789cc97e8e6832ac239d9c6b5d7df4e83b4680c10d7b977a24ef77a5808be",
      "text_span": [
        0,
        390
      ],
      "version": "TRD-v0.4"
    },
    "policy_f88b78f11e4561f77dd866f4": {
      "authority": "PRODUCT_POLICY",
      "evidence_id": "policy_f88b78f11e4561f77dd866f4",
      "exact_text": "Document diagrams: associate image with figure, heading, parent procedure and original page crop; require model verification against the image for image-dependent claims",
      "paragraph_index": 147,
      "source_path": "03_TRD.docx",
      "source_sha256": "aeedf6789ddfbddc674c1926c5d4441a27708bd260c673d876a5ff7fdb3792ac",
      "text_sha256": "6f9653362bcea02c3055be7f5d468866a7d28f44cdbe0fadf9cdaf8acb105e43",
      "text_span": [
        0,
        169
      ],
      "version": "TRD-v0.4"
    },
    "policy_fd0622ee416c74c87cbaf0d6": {
      "authority": "PRODUCT_POLICY",
      "evidence_id": "policy_fd0622ee416c74c87cbaf0d6",
      "exact_text": "Even a high-scoring semantic verifier can make mistakes; guarantee only that the application follows the fail-closed protocol, not that all semantic classifications are infallible. Output citations must map to immutable evidence object IDs, not model-created page numbers.",
      "paragraph_index": 144,
      "source_path": "03_TRD.docx",
      "source_sha256": "aeedf6789ddfbddc674c1926c5d4441a27708bd260c673d876a5ff7fdb3792ac",
      "text_sha256": "1b92e5c37964e983e1ba3f03392b16d6edad587a65655a3764d36d5b1a0a38a3",
      "text_span": [
        0,
